1. DEFINITIONS

  - Host: A device on which the Software (server) is installed and provides
    remote control (e.g., a macOS device).
  - Client: A device/app that remotely connects to a Host.
  - Seat: A unit of usage rights for one Host under a license.
  - License Holder: The user registered to a license (e.g., name + email).
  - Activation: The act of registering/linking a license to a specific Host.
  - Concurrent Connections: The number of Clients simultaneously connected
    to a single Host.


2. GRANT OF LICENSE

The Company grants you a non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable
license to use the Software, subject to the terms of this agreement and
purchase conditions.

The Software is licensed, not sold.


3. LICENSE TYPES AND SCOPE OF USE

The Software is provided under one of the license types below. Specific terms
displayed on the purchase screen, invoice, or management page shall take
precedence over this section, which serves as a summary.

3.1 Full License

  - Purchase model: One-time purchase (perpetual license)
  - Seats allowed: Up to 2 Hosts per license
  - Concurrent connections: Up to 2 Clients per Host
  - Update policy: This license covers versions v1.0.0 through less than
    v2.0.0. To use v2.0.0 or later (including subsequent major updates),
    a discounted upgrade license (separate purchase) from the Company may
    be required.
  - Support: Email support

3.2 Trial License

  - Duration: Up to 7 days
  - Seats allowed: 1 Host per License Holder
  - Issuance limit: Once per License Holder
  - The Company may restrict or deny trial license issuance to prevent abuse.


4. SEATS / ACTIVATION / REVOCATION

  - Licenses have seat (Host count) limits. Once the limit is reached, no
    further activations are possible.
  - You may revoke the activation of a specific Host through the management
    page or procedures provided by the Company.
  - The Company may request additional verification or restrict activations
    if abuse or abnormal activation patterns are detected.


