9. DATA AND TELEMETRY

The Company processes data as described below for the proper operation and
improvement of the Software. For details, refer to the Privacy Policy.

9.1 License Authentication Data

  - To verify licenses and prevent unauthorized copying, a Device Identifier
    is transmitted to and stored on team unstablers Inc. servers when a
    license is activated.
  - The Device Identifier is retained until the license is revoked
    (deactivated) on that device.

9.2 Telemetry and Error Reporting

  - The Software includes built-in telemetry to assist with development and
    quality improvement.
  - This feature is OFF by default for privacy protection and only operates
    when the user explicitly enables it (opt-in) in the settings.
  - Data collected: OS version, error messages, stack traces, and comparable
    program execution context information.
  - Privacy protection:
      - Personally identifiable information (PII) is transmitted in a
        masked state.
      - Data is transmitted on a session basis with a randomly assigned
        identifier, which the user may reset at any time.
  - Storage and retention: Collected data is stored in Sentry US Region
    and deleted after a maximum of 6 months.
  - Regional restriction: Telemetry cannot be enabled on devices whose
    macOS region setting corresponds to a country within the European
    Economic Area (EEA) or the United Kingdom.


